# Code owners for review requirements (RFP §11).
#
# There is one maintainer at the moment, so there is nothing for this file
# to enforce: GitHub cannot require a review from the person who opened the
# pull request. The rules are kept here, commented out, rather than deleted
# — the paths are the argument, and they stay correct whoever ends up
# owning them.
#
# To switch them on, uncomment and replace OWNER with a username
# (@someone) or a team (@org/maintainers).

# The timing engine and the decoder. §11: "a contributor can break these in
# ways nobody notices until copy accuracy quietly degrades."
# /src/core/timing.ts        OWNER
# /src/core/decoder.ts       OWNER

# The export envelope is a contract with Phase 2, which is required to read
# every version this one writes.
# /src/storage/schema.ts     OWNER

# Build and release scripts, and the workflows themselves.
# /scripts/                  OWNER
# /.github/                  OWNER

# Phase 2, listed ahead of time so the rule is already in force when the
# code arrives rather than being remembered afterwards.
# /src/auth/                 OWNER
# /src/signalling/           OWNER
# /server/                   OWNER
